WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:04.804
SPEAKER:<i> Ladies and gentlemen,
 this is your "places" call.</i>

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.605
<i> Places for the coming show.</i>

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:09.009
(APPLAUSE)

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.144
JONATHAN GROFF: Spring Awakening
<i> is so hard to describe.</i>

00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:14.881 line:0%
1891 Germany. Rock music.
There's children in it.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:18.951
LAUREN PRITCHARD-COBB:
<i> The gay scene. Abortion.
 The sex. The suicide.</i>

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:20.820 line:0%
<i> There was never
 anything like this</i>

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.355 line:0%
that's ever happened on stage.

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:24.523
TOM HULCE:
<i> The controversial nature meant</i>

00:00:24.623 --> 00:00:27.527 line:0%
that we never thought
about Broadway.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:28.861 line:0%
But it touched a nerve.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.497 line:0%
We became rock stars.

00:00:32.998 --> 00:00:34.534
(CHEERING, APPLAUSE)

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:41.740
Getting back together after
50 years is gonna be insane.

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:42.842
We did it!

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:43.810
(LAUGHS)

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:48.714
For the years we worked on it,
we were rejected everywhere

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.483
and everyone thought
we were out of our minds.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:56.222 line:0%
When we were in previews,
we were losing money big time.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.857
<i> It was a disaster.</i>

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.191 line:0%
It really didn't start well.

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:00.659
Michael said to the cast,

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.862
<i> "The future of this
 is in your hands."</i>

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:06.066
<i> And that night something
 happened in that theater.</i>

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:12.671
<i> ♪ Oh, the wonder ♪</i>

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:16.275
<i> ♪ I will sing ♪</i>

00:01:16.575 --> 00:01:20.713
<i> ♪ The song of purple summer ♪</i>

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:24.183
If you were able to see
<i> Spring Awakening</i>
at the Atlantic Theater,

00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:26.252 line:0%
you got to see something
very special.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.687 line:0%
People were
jumping for joy and shouting.

00:01:28.787 --> 00:01:29.955
<i> It was totally surreal.</i>

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:31.390 line:0%
It felt like
we were The Beatles.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:36.629
We, of course,
loved our show and loved
playing our characters,

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:40.199
<i> but the real fun we had
 was off-stage together.</i>

00:01:40.632 --> 00:01:42.602
SPEAKER 2:<i> Through the cast
 and through the opportunity</i>

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.670
<i> of getting to play
 this character,</i>

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.707
<i> I had grown this strength...</i>

00:01:48.874 --> 00:01:50.443
and it changed my life.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.746
<i> ♪ God is this it? ♪</i>

00:01:54.379 --> 00:02:00.353
<i> ♪ This can't be it! ♪</i>

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.055
<i> ♪ Oh, God!
 What a bitch! ♪</i>

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.459
SPEAKER 3:<i> The things
 that we confront in this show</i>

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.094
<i> are not things
 you can learn in school.</i>

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.762
And they're things
that help people survive.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:12.264
SPEAKER 4:<i> That's kind of what
 got us through it every night,</i>

00:02:12.364 --> 00:02:14.701
knowing how important
it was to tell that story.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.303
SPEAKER 5:
<i>This was not about this reunion.</i>

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:23.243
This was an opportunity
to be with those kids
and see who they've become.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:28.281
I would not have
survived the experience,
if it wasn't for all of you.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.152
I learned
that dreams can come true.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.389
(APPLAUSE)

